35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings show that transport costs are highly volatile and can easily become the largest expense. Additionally, public bookings involve a rigid, high-effort application process that leaves very little room for error or flexibility.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My research indicates that relying on our own facilities would severely disrupt our training schedule. Furthermore, self-catering is a significant drain on the organizers' time and energy, which we must avoid this year.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data confirms my concerns. A significant number of members are dropping out, and the only way to foster genuine interaction between year-groups is to ensure everyone stays in the same facility. We must prioritize shared living.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I've found that some inland options can be quite crowded, with many people sharing a single room. Also, a third of our members struggle with early travel, which could lead to exhaustion before the camp even begins.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My research shows that whole-building lets carry a high financial risk; non-refundable deposits mean the remaining members must cover the cost of any late cancellations. Conversely, public beds offer a very stable, flat per-person rate.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, while public beds seem stable per person, the lottery process is a nightmare. If we miss a date, we risk everything. We need a balance between price stability and a guaranteed booking to avoid financial chaos.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, I agree. A high-risk booking process adds unnecessary stress. However, we must also prioritize a destination with provided meals. If we choose a place requiring self-catering, the organizers will be exhausted before training even starts.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, I understand the burden of labor, but we cannot prioritize convenience over the club's survival. If we don't fix the social divide now, we will continue losing members. We need a facility that mandates shared space.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I understand the need for bonding, but we must be careful. If we force everyone into crowded rooms, the lack of sleep will lead to irritability and tension, which could actually damage our cohesion further.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, you make a valid point. However, we must also consider the financial tension. If we choose a whole-building let and people cancel, the resulting cost increase for those who attend will create a different kind of resentment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka @Toshio, we must avoid any option where the final cost is unpredictable or the administrative risk is too high. A deficit is unacceptable. We need a destination with fixed costs and a reliable booking method.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, I agree. But we must also ensure the on-site workload is minimal. If we prioritize a fixed cost but end up with heavy cooking duties, the organizers will pay a price that isn't reflected in the budget.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, labor is a temporary burden, but the loss of members is permanent. We must choose a place where the layout forces interaction. A facility with shared living spaces is non-negotiable if we want to stop the attrition.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree that interaction is vital, but quality of rest is a fundamental need. If we prioritize shared spaces at the expense of sleep, we risk a camp where everyone is too exhausted to actually bond.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, forcing interaction is useless if the members are resentful. If we choose a facility with a rigid flat fee and people drop out, the financial burden on those remaining will create more division than any shared living space can fix.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka @Minako, we are circling the same problem. We need a solution that balances social goals with financial certainty. Let's look for an option that avoids both the lottery risk and the non-refundable deposit trap.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, exactly. We must also ensure the option doesn't shift the burden to on-site labor. A destination that provides meals and has a straightforward booking process is the only way to protect the organizers' well-being.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji @Toshio, I understand your concerns, but we cannot ignore the attrition rate. If we prioritize only convenience and cost, we are managing a club that is slowly disappearing. We must choose the option that best facilitates shared living.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe we must find a middle ground. If we prioritize shared living but sacrifice sleep and recovery, we will only increase the members' stress. Let's look for an option that balances cohesion with actual comfort.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji @Minako, the most logical path is to avoid any arrangement where the cost per person fluctuates based on attendance. We need a per-head pricing model to ensure fairness and prevent financial resentment among the members.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
